<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">APPENDIX</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Policy Gradient Methods:</span> Majority of the existing literature on policy gradient methods in the context of generative modeling draw inspiration from Proximal Policy Optimization(PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and REINFORCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>. PPO based methods in the context of language modeling include <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al. [2]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al. [3]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. [38]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stiennon et al. [14]</a></cite>, whereas frameworks based on REINFORCE include <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>. Policy gradient methods have also been studied in the context of fine-tuning diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Offline Fine-Tuning Methods:</span> Algorithms which utilize offline preference datasets for fine-tuning generative models have also been widely studied. In the context of language modeling, these include methods like SLiC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> and SimPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. Such methods have also been explore in the context of diffusion models as well - these include methods like Diffusion-DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite> and Diffusion-KTO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rejection Sampling Methods:</span> Recently, many works have explored rejection sampling methods in the context of autoregressive models - these include RSO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, RAFT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> and Reinforce-Rej <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. In particular, Reinforce-Rej demonstrated that rejection sampling methods can match or even outperform policy gradient methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models:</span> Apart from the policy gradient methods discussed already, a host of other methods have also been proposed for fine-tuning diffusion models. Direct reward backpropagation methods include DRaFT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> and VADER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>. Note that these methods assume access to a differentiable reward. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Uehara et al. [8]</a></cite> approaches the problem from the lens of entropy-regularized control - however, the method is computationally heavy and requires gradient checkpointing as well as optimizing an additional neural SDE. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Domingo-Enrich et al. [7]</a></cite> proposes a memoryless forward process to overcome the initial value function bias problem for the case of ODEs. PRDP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> formulates a supervised learning objective whose optimum matches with the solution to PPO, but with trajectory KL constraint - the supervised objective, with clipping, was found to make the training stable as compared to DDPO.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score Matching:</span>
Score matching for distribution estimation was first introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>. The algorithm used in this case is called Implicit Score Matching. Diffusion models primarily use Denoising Score Matching (DSM), which is based on Tweedie’s formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. The sample complexity of DSM has been extensively studied in the literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.Many alternative procedures such as Sliced Score Matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite> and Target Score Matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> have been proposed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ODE Reversal in Flow Models:</span> A prominent use case of ODE reversal in flow models is that of image editing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>, <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. The reverse ODE has also been used to achieve straighter flows, allowing for faster generation, through 2-rectification/reflow algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>, <a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>. Notably, concurrent work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite> also proposes a strategy for aligning distilled models by fine-tuning at the noise level.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>ODE Solver Algorithms</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the backward Euler Algorithm <a href="#alg6" title="Algorithm 6 ‣ Appendix B ODE Solver Algorithms ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, at each time instant <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in the reverse procedure, we solve a fixed point equation to obtain high precision solution of Eq. (<a href="#S5.E5" title="In 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The step-size <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is tuned empirically so that the recursion does not blow up. Once the step-size is carefully tuned, the iteration converges to the solution at an exponential rate. In practice, we observed that <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{b}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{b}=10</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficient to obtain satisfactory results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg5" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:148.3pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span> Forward Euler (FWD_Euler)</figcaption>
<div id="alg5.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg5.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Flow model <math id="alg5.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, step-size <math id="alg5.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, Initial point <math id="alg5.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           

</div>
<div id="alg5.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg5.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg5.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg5.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg5.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg5.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg5.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j+1}\leftarrow X_{j}+\eta v_{\theta}(X_{j},\eta j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j+1}\leftarrow X_{j}+\eta v_{\theta}(X_{j},\eta j)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg5.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg5.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg5.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg5.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg6" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 6</span> </span> Backward Euler (BWD_Euler)</figcaption>
<div id="alg6.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg6.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Flow model <math id="alg6.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, step size <math id="alg6.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="alg6.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> from the dataset, Number of fixed point iterations <math id="alg6.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           

</div>
<div id="alg6.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <math id="alg6.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{1}=X^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{1}=X^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg6.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg6.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg6.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg6.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{0}=X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{0}=X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg6.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg6.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{b}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{b}-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg6.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg6.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg6.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{k+1}\leftarrow X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j}-\eta v_{\theta}(\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{k},1-\eta(j+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{k+1}\leftarrow X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j}-\eta v_{\theta}(\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{k},1-\eta(j+1))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg6.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg6.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j+1}\leftarrow\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{N_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{j+1}\leftarrow\hat{X}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{N_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg6.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg6.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg6.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg6.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg6.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg6.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\lfloor 1/\eta\rfloor}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>GRAFT: Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While instantiations of GRAFT are well-known in the literature and are straightforward to implement, we provide the exact algorithm here for the sake of completeness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg7" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 7</span> </span> GRAFT: Training</figcaption>
<div id="alg7.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg7.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           Trainable <math id="alg7.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reference <math id="alg7.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reward function <math id="alg7.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, Acceptance function <math id="alg7.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, Number of sampling rounds <math id="alg7.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
            
            
           

</div>
<div id="alg7.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Initialize empty set <math id="alg7.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg7.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg7.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg7.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg7.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg7.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Get <math id="alg7.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> samples: <math id="alg7.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{(1)},\dots,X^{(M)}\}\sim\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{(1)},\dots,X^{(M)}\}\sim\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            Obtain rewards: <math id="alg7.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(X^{(i)})\,;\quad i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(X^{(i)})\,;\quad i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Perform GRS using acceptance function <math id="alg7.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to get accepted samples <math id="alg7.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            Perform <math id="alg7.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}\;\cup\;\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}\;\cup\;\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg7.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg7.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg7.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
           Train <math id="alg7.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg7.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg7.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg7.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg7.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3 GRAFT: Generalized Rejection sAmpling Fine Tuning ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be any measurable set. Consider the following probability measure:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B|X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B|X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using Bayes’ rule, this measure can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B|X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B|X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})}{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})}{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn from the distribution <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, from the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}|X^{(1)}=x)d\bar{p}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}|X^{(1)}=x)d\bar{p}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">From Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1. ‣ 3 GRAFT: Generalized Rejection sAmpling Fine Tuning ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we know that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x)d\bar{p}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x)d\bar{p}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbbm{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the indicator function. Using the tower property of expectations, this can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in B,X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)},\dots,X^{(M)})\right]\bigr|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)},\dots,X^{(M)})\right]\bigr|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{P}\left(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)},\dots,X^{(M)}\right)\bigr|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{P}\left(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)},\dots,X^{(M)}\right)\bigr|X^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Note that in the conditional expectation here, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)},\dots,X^{(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)},\dots,X^{(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, are distributed according to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d samples. Again, from Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 3.1. ‣ 3 GRAFT: Generalized Rejection sAmpling Fine Tuning ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we know that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x,\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{M})=A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}=x,\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{M})=A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed using the samples <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From definition of Radon-Nikodym derivative, the distribution of the accepted samples can therefore be written as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{p}^{a}(x)=Z_{1}\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x\right]\bar{p}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{p}^{a}(x)=Z_{1}\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x\right]\bar{p}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}=1/\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}=1/\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalizing constant independent of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, from the method of Lagrangian Multipliers, as mentioned in Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the solution to the PPO optimization objective with reward function <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p}^{\text{ppo}}(x)=Z_{2}\exp\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}\right)\bar{p}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>ppo</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p}^{\text{ppo}}(x)=Z_{2}\exp\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}\right)\bar{p}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization constant. Comparing (<a href="#A4.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ D.1 Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ D.1 Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}^{a}=p^{\text{ppo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>ppo</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}^{a}=p^{\text{ppo}}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X}|X^{(1)}=x\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X}|X^{(1)}=x\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Instantiations of GRAFT</h3>

<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Top-<math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> out of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> sampling</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{n}}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x,\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{M}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{n}}\left[A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x,\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{M}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we get:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\left(\int_{\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{n}}\mathbbm{1}(r(x)\in\mathsf{Top-K}(r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)})))d\bar{p}(x^{(2)})\dots d\bar{p}(x^{(M)})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝗈𝗉</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\left(\int_{\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=2}^{n}}\mathbbm{1}(r(x)\in\mathsf{Top-K}(r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)})))d\bar{p}(x^{(2)})\dots d\bar{p}(x^{(M)})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Top-K}(r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝗈𝗉</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Top-K}(r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)}))</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the top-<math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> samples in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r(x),r(x^{(2)}),\dots,r(x^{(M)})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)}=x</annotation></semantics></math> ranks in top-<math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> among the <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> samples, where the other <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M-1</annotation></semantics></math> samples are i.i.d from <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. This event can be decomposed as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle U_{K}=\cup_{k=1}^{K}E_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{K}=\cup_{k=1}^{K}E_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the event where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the ranked (descending) ordering of rewards. Further, note that <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{E_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{E_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">mutually exclusive</span> events. Therefore:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(U_{K})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{P}(E_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(U_{K})=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{P}(E_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computing <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>:</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> ranks <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> when ranked in terms of rewards, there are <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> samples which have <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">higher</span> rewards than <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M-k</annotation></semantics></math> samples which have <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lower</span> rewards than <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the required probability can be computed by finding the probability of having <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math> samples having higher rewards and the rest having lower rewards. Note that the ordering within the <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math> group or <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M-K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M-K</annotation></semantics></math> group doesn’t matter. The probability of any one sample having a higher reward than <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-F(r({x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-F(r({x}))</annotation></semantics></math> and having a lower reward is <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(r({x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(r({x}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the required probability can be computed as:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{k})=\binom{M-1}{k-1}(1-F(r({x})))^{k-1}(F(r({x})))^{M-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{k})=\binom{M-1}{k-1}(1-F(r({x})))^{k-1}(F(r({x})))^{M-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">And hence:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(U_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(U_{K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\binom{M-1}{k}(1-F(r({x})))^{k}(F(r({x})))^{M-k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\binom{M-1}{k}(1-F(r({x})))^{k}(F(r({x})))^{M-k-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\binom{M-1}{k}(1-F(r({x})))^{k}(F(r({x})))^{M-k-1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{k=0}^{K-1}\binom{M-1}{k}(1-F(r({x})))^{k}(F(r({x})))^{M-k-1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that this is an increasing function in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.2 </span>Preference Rewards</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{X^{(2)}}A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\left(\mathbb{E}_{X^{(2)}}A(r(x),\hat{F}_{R}(r(x)),x,\hat{P}_{X})|X^{(1)}=x,X^{(2)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we get:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\left(\int_{X^{(2)}}\mathbbm{1}(r(x^{(2)})\leq r(x))d\bar{p}(x^{(2)})\right)=\log F(r(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\left(\int_{X^{(2)}}\mathbbm{1}(r(x^{(2)})\leq r(x))d\bar{p}(x^{(2)})\right)=\log F(r(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2. ‣ 4 Partial-GRAFT for Diffusion Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be any measurable set. Consider the following probability measure:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B|X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B|X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using Bayes’ rule, this measure can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B|X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B|X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})}{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})}{\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn from the distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, from the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}|X^{(1)}_{t}=x)d\bar{p}_{t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}|X^{(1)}_{t}=x)d\bar{p}_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 4.1. ‣ 4 Partial-GRAFT for Diffusion Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we know that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X^{(1)}_{t}\in B,X^{(1)}_{t}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}_{t}=x)d\bar{p}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X^{(1)}_{t}=x)d\bar{p}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbbm{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the indicator function. Using the tower property of expectations, this can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X_{t}^{(1)}\in B,X_{t}^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(X_{t}^{(1)}\in B,X_{t}^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,X_{0}^{(1)},X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)})\right]\bigr|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[(\mathbbm{1}(C_{1}=1)|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,X_{0}^{(1)},X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)})\right]\bigr|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{P}\left(C_{1}=1|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,X_{0}^{(1)},X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)}\right)\bigr|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbb{P}\left(C_{1}=1|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,X_{0}^{(1)},X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)}\right)\bigr|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]d\bar{p}_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that in the conditional expectation here, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}^{(2)},\dots,X_{0}^{(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>, are distributed according to <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{0}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{0}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d samples. However, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed according to <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math> because of the conditioning on <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, from Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 4.1. ‣ 4 Partial-GRAFT for Diffusion Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we know that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,\{X_{0}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M})=A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(C_{1}=1|X_{t}^{(1)}=x,\{X_{0}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M})=A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed using the samples <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the definition of Radon-Nikodym derivative, the density of the accepted samples can therefore be written as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{p}^{a}_{t}(x)=Z_{1}\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X}|X_{t}^{(1)}=x)\right]\bar{p}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{p}^{a}_{t}(x)=Z_{1}\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X}|X_{t}^{(1)}=x)\right]\bar{p}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}=1/\mathbb{P}(X_{t}^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}=1/\mathbb{P}(X_{t}^{(1)}\in\mathcal{A}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalizing constant independent of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, from the method of Lagrangian Multipliers, as mentioned in Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the solution to the PPO optimization objective (with reward function <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>) is (where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization constant):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{p}^{\text{ppo}}(x)=Z_{2}\exp\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}\right)\bar{p}_{t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>ppo</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{p}^{\text{ppo}}(x)=Z_{2}\exp\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}\right)\bar{p}_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Comparing (<a href="#A4.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}^{a}_{t}=p^{\text{ppo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>ppo</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}^{a}_{t}=p^{\text{ppo}}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\hat{r}(x)}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X}|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>X</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\mathbb{E}\left[A(r(X_{0}^{(1)}),\hat{F}_{R}(r(X_{0}^{(1)})),X_{0}^{(1)},\hat{P}_{X}|X_{t}^{(1)}=x\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.1 A Bias-Variance Tradeoff Justification for P-GRAFT ‣ 4 Partial-GRAFT for Diffusion Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s}\to X_{t}\to X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s}\to X_{t}\to X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a Markov chain. By the law of total variance, we have for any random variables <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y,Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{Var}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{Var}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\mathsf{Var}(Z|Y)+\mathsf{Var}(\mathbb{E}[Z|Y])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\mathsf{Var}(Z|Y)+\mathsf{Var}(\mathbb{E}[Z|Y])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}\mathsf{Var}(Z|Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}\mathsf{Var}(Z|Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, Suppose <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z,Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z,Y</annotation></semantics></math> be jointly distributed as the law of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r(X_{0}),X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r(X_{0}),X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{s})\geq\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{s},X_{t})|X_{s}]=\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{t})|X_{s}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖺𝗋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{s})\geq\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{s},X_{t})|X_{s}]=\mathbb{E}[\mathsf{Var}(r(X_{0})|X_{t})|X_{s}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the last line, we have used the Markov property to show that the law of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(X_{0})|X_{s},X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(X_{0})|X_{s},X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the law of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(X_{0})|X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(X_{0})|X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. We conclude the result by taking expectation over both the sides.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.1 A Bias-Variance Tradeoff Justification for P-GRAFT ‣ 4 Partial-GRAFT for Diffusion Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will follow the exposition in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite> for our proofs.
<math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>, Lemma 2]</cite> applied to the forward process, we conclude that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}dXq_{t}(X)\|\nabla\log q_{t}(X)-\nabla\log q_{\infty}(X)\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}dXq_{t}(X)\|\nabla\log q_{t}(X)-\nabla\log q_{\infty}(X)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\implies\int_{t}^{T}dt\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}dXq_{s}(X)\|\nabla\log q_{s}(X)-\nabla\log q_{\infty}(X)\|^{2}=\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})-\mathsf{KL}(q_{T}||q_{\infty})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies\int_{t}^{T}dt\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}dXq_{s}(X)\|\nabla\log q_{s}(X)-\nabla\log q_{\infty}(X)\|^{2}=\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})-\mathsf{KL}(q_{T}||q_{\infty})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For brevity, we call the LHS to be <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{t}^{T}-e^{-2t}H_{0}^{T}=\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})-e^{-2t}\mathsf{KL}(q_{0}||q_{\infty})+\mathsf{KL}(q_{T}||q_{\infty})(e^{-2t}-1)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}^{T}-e^{-2t}H_{0}^{T}=\mathsf{KL}(q_{t}||q_{\infty})-e^{-2t}\mathsf{KL}(q_{0}||q_{\infty})+\mathsf{KL}(q_{T}||q_{\infty})(e^{-2t}-1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is the density of the standard Gaussian random variable. Therefore, it satisfies the Gaussian Logarithmic Sobolev inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>. Thus, we can apply <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>, Theorem 4]</cite> to conclude that for every <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}(q_{s}||q_{\infty})\leq e^{-2s}\mathsf{KL}(q_{0}||q_{\infty})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}(q_{s}||q_{\infty})\leq e^{-2s}\mathsf{KL}(q_{0}||q_{\infty})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}^{T}\leq\frac{e^{-2t}}{1-e^{-2t}}H_{0}^{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}^{T}\leq\frac{e^{-2t}}{1-e^{-2t}}H_{0}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The uniqueness and the convergence of fixed point iteration for implicit Euler methods have been established under great generality in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>. However, we give a simpler proof for our specialized setting here.</p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the update for the backward Euler iteration at each time step <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\eta i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\eta i</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i}\rightarrow\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}-\eta v_{\theta}(\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i},1-\eta(i-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i}\rightarrow\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}-\eta v_{\theta}(\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i},1-\eta(i-1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let us define an operator <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x)=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}-\eta v_{\theta}(x,1-\eta(i-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x)=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}-\eta v_{\theta}(x,1-\eta(i-1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">First, we will show that <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined above is a contractive operator under the condition <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta L&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta L&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, one can use Banach fixed point theorem to establish uniqueness of the solution and obtain the solution through fixed point iteration. To this end, consider two point <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and apply <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> to them</p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{1})-T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{2})\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{1})-T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{2})\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\|v_{\theta}(x_{1},1-\eta(i-1))-v_{\theta}(x_{2},1-\eta(i-1))\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\|v_{\theta}(x_{1},1-\eta(i-1))-v_{\theta}(x_{2},1-\eta(i-1))\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\eta L\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\eta L\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta L&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta L&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contractive operator. Thus, by Banach fixed point theorem, the fixed point equation <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique solution for each step <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\eta i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\eta i</annotation></semantics></math>. To obtain the solution to the backward Euler update, we use the Banach fixed point method, i.e., start with <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(0)}=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(0)}=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> (or any arbitrary point in <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>) and run the iteration <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(k+1)}=T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(k+1)}=T_{\theta,\eta}^{\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta(i-1)}}(x_{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}x_{(k)}=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}x_{(k)}=\hat{x}^{\mathsf{rev}}_{\eta i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The invertibility of the operator <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from the previous part. Since the solution for the backward Euler method is unique at each time step <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\eta i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\eta i</annotation></semantics></math>, it implies that there exists a one-to-one mapping between sample points <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before starting the proof of this lemma, we will state the following well-known theorem from information theory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[Date Processing Inequality]
Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be two sample spaces. Denote <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of all possible probability distributions on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X},Q_{X}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X},Q_{X}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Y|X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Y|X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a transition kernel. Denote <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the push through, i.e., <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Y}(B)=\int_{\mathcal{X}}P_{Y|X}(B|X=x)dP_{X}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Y}(B)=\int_{\mathcal{X}}P_{Y|X}(B|X=x)dP_{X}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{f}(P_{X}||Q_{X})\geq D_{f}(P_{Y}|Q_{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{f}(P_{X}||Q_{X})\geq D_{f}(P_{Y}|Q_{Y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By part 3 of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we have that <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}=T_{\theta,\eta}^{-1}(x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}})\implies T_{\theta,\eta}(x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}})=x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}=T_{\theta,\eta}^{-1}(x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}})\implies T_{\theta,\eta}(x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}})=x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}\sim p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathsf{rev}}\sim p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then by definition, <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}\sim p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}\sim p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the result.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm is an <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence. Furthermore, <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the push forward function from <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Thus, using DPI <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}},p_{0})\geq\mathsf{TV}(p^{*},p_{1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}},p_{0})\geq\mathsf{TV}(p^{*},p_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Additionally, <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is an invertible mapping. Hence, <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\theta,\eta}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\theta,\eta}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> can also be viewed as the push forward function from <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Thus, again using DPI <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, we get</p>
<table id="A4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(p^{*},p_{1})\geq\mathsf{TV}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}},p_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(p^{*},p_{1})\geq\mathsf{TV}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}},p_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Combining both the bounds, we get the desired claim.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KL divergence is also a valid <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence. Thus, repeating the arguments from the previous part, one gets the desired equality.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.8 </span>Theoretical Justification for Inverse Noise Correction</h3>

<div id="A4.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to provide a theoretical justification for inverse noise correction in the context of flow models. Specifically, we will argue that if <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,\textbf{I}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,\textbf{I}))</annotation></semantics></math> is small, then it is less challenging to learn the score function corresponding to <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and thereby the velocity field <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{X}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{X}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> governing the rectified flow. To this end, let <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a sample from a distribution <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z,Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z,Y</annotation></semantics></math> be standard normal random variables all independent of each other. Consider the following two linear interpolations:</p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A4.EGx39" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="4"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E14.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}=tX+(1-t)Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}=tX+(1-t)Z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E14.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{t}=tY+(1-t)Z." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{t}=tY+(1-t)Z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Denote <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the distribution of <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Then, it is easy to verify that they satisfy the following continuity equations:</p>
<table id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A4.EGx40" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="4"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E15.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{p_{t}}+\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{X}p_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{p_{t}}+\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{X}p_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.E15.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{q_{t}}+\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{Y}q_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{q_{t}}+\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{Y}q_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{X}(x)=\mathbb{E}[X-Z|X_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{X}(x)=\mathbb{E}[X-Z|X_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}(x)=\mathbb{E}[Y-Z|Y_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}(x)=\mathbb{E}[Y-Z|Y_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have the following theorem which establishes the relation between KL-divergence of <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the velocities <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof for the theorem is provided in Section <a href="#A4.SS9" title="D.9 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the distribution of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A4.E14" title="In D.8 Theoretical Justification for Inverse Noise Correction ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>). Then, the KL-divergence between <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the following relation</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}||q_{1})=\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}||q_{1})=\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, consider the distribution of the inverse noise <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by iterating (<a href="#S5.E5" title="In 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and substitute it with <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}</annotation></semantics></math> in the theorem above. Suppose that the flow model is trained such that <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}(p^{\text{data}}||p_{1})\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}(p^{\text{data}}||p_{1})\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5 Inverse Noise Correction for Flow Models ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> it follows that <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}||p_{0})\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}||p_{0})\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this observation with (<a href="#A4.E16" title="In Theorem D.2. ‣ D.8 Theoretical Justification for Inverse Noise Correction ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), it is easy to see that the velocities <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{X}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{X}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> should be close to each other. Additionally, since <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> simply corresponds to learning a flow model from standard Gaussian to itself, we can explicitly compute <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{t}^{Y}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{t}^{Y}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\frac{-x}{(1-t)^{2}+t^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\frac{-x}{(1-t)^{2}+t^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{x(2t-1)}{(1-t)^{2}+t^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{x(2t-1)}{(1-t)^{2}+t^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear function of <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and a rational function of <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}||p_{0})\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗏</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}^{\mathsf{rev}}||p_{0})\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem D.2. ‣ D.8 Theoretical Justification for Inverse Noise Correction ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> suggests that learning <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{X}</annotation></semantics></math> from data should be relatively easier as it is close to <math id="A4.SS8.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.9 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem D.2. ‣ D.8 Theoretical Justification for Inverse Noise Correction ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then, the time derivative of the KL-divergence between <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{d}{dt}\left(p_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)\right)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{d}{dt}\left(p_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)\right)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left(\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)+p_{t}(x)\frac{d}{dt}\log(p_t(x))-p_{t}(x)\frac{d}{dt}\log(q_t(x))\right)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left(\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)+p_{t}(x)\frac{d}{dt}\log(p_t(x))-p_{t}(x)\frac{d}{dt}\log(q_t(x))\right)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left(\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)+\dot{p}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)\frac{\dot{q}_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left(\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)+\dot{p}_{t}(x)-p_{t}(x)\frac{\dot{q}_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We will consider each term separately as <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1},T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1},T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> using the continuity equation, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dot{p}_{t}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{X}(x)p_{t}(x))\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{X}(x)p_{t}(x))\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle v_{t}^{X}(x),\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)\right\rangle dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle v_{t}^{X}(x),\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right)\right\rangle dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Integration by parts)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)dx=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)dx=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus for <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex9a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{2}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dot{p}_{t}(x)dx=\frac{d}{dt}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)dx=\frac{d}{dt}1=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{2}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dot{p}_{t}(x)dx=\frac{d}{dt}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)dx=\frac{d}{dt}1=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For the final term <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we again use the continuity equation to get</p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10a.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\frac{\dot{q}_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\frac{\dot{q}_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\frac{\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{Y}q_{t})}{q_{t}(x)}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\frac{\nabla\cdot(v_{t}^{Y}q_{t})}{q_{t}(x)}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex12a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}q_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}q_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Integration by parts)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex13a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex13a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Combining all the terms above, we get</p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\nabla\log\left(\frac{p_{t}(x)}{q_{t}(x)}\right),v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.6" class="ltx_p">To obtain an expression for score function in terms of the velocity vector, we use Tweedie’s formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite> which leads us to</p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X-Z|X_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X-Z|X_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}\mathbb{E}[X-X_{t}|X_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}\mathbb{E}[X-X_{t}|X_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex15a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex15a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}\mathbb{E}[X|X_{t}=x]-\frac{x}{1-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}\mathbb{E}[X|X_{t}=x]-\frac{x}{1-t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex17a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex17a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{t(1-t)}\left(x+(1-t)^{2}\nabla\log p_{t}(x)\right)-\frac{x}{1-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{t(1-t)}\left(x+(1-t)^{2}\nabla\log p_{t}(x)\right)-\frac{x}{1-t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\nabla\log p_{t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\nabla\log p_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle v_{t}^{Y}(x)=\mathbb{E}[Y-Z|Y_{t}=x]=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\nabla\log q_{t}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{t}^{Y}(x)=\mathbb{E}[Y-Z|Y_{t}=x]=\frac{x}{t}+\frac{1-t}{t}\nabla\log q_{t}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Plugging in the expressions for the score functions into (<a href="#A4.E17" title="In D.9 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex18a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex18a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\mathsf{KL}(p_{t}||q_{t})}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex18a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\frac{t}{1-t}\left(v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right),v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\langle\frac{t}{1-t}\left(v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right),v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\rangle dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex19a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex20a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\implies\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}||q_{1})-\mathsf{KL}(p_{0}||q_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies\mathsf{KL}(p_{1}||q_{1})-\mathsf{KL}(p_{0}||q_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS9.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}=q_{0}=q_{1}=\mathcal{N}(0,\textbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}=q_{0}=q_{1}=\mathcal{N}(0,\textbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS9.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}=p^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}=p^{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we get the desired claim</p>
<table id="A4.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex21a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(p^{X}||\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{t}{1-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p_{t}(x)\left\|v_{t}^{X}(x)-v_{t}^{Y}(x)\right\|^{2}dxdt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Text-to-Image Generation</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Ablations</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1 </span>Different choices of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report results for various choices of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Top-K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝗈𝗉</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Top-K}</annotation></semantics></math> of M sampling for GenAI-Bench in Tables <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Note that these models are also trained on GenAI-Bench. We also report the (mean)score separately for the “Basic" and “Advanced" split in the prompt set. Results for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Top-10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝗈𝗉</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟣𝟢</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Top-10}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> sampling for T2I-CompBench++ is given in Table <a href="#A5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Models for Table <a href="#A5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> were trained on the train split of T2I-CompBench++. All results are consistent with the developed theory: both GRAFT and P-GRAFT outperform base SDv2 and P-GRAFT, for an appropriate choice of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> always outperform GRAFT.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>VQAScore on GenAI-Bench for <math id="A5.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=4</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
