<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Compute FLOPs Analysis of P-GRAFT</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare the compute cost of P-GRAFT and DDPO in terms of total UNet FLOPs.
Let <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the cost of one UNet forward pass at <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64{\times}64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64{\times}64</annotation></semantics></math> latent resolution. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kaplan et al. [72]</a></cite>, we approximate a backward training step 2 times of a forward step. So if <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the forward step compute, a forward + backward step will incur <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3F_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3F_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume a batch size of <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> for both algorithms for standardization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> prompts, <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> samples per prompt, top-<math id="A5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> retained, <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> diffusion steps, <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{sft}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>sft</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{sft}}</annotation></semantics></math> epochs. For the implementation we use the standard stable diffusion training script that only samples a single timestep <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> during training:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathrm{P\text{-}GRAFT}}=\underbrace{P\,M\,T}_{\text{sampling}}\,F_{u}\;+\;\underbrace{E_{\mathrm{sft}}\,P\,K}_{\text{ training}}3F_{u}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>GRAFT</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>sampling</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>sft</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext> training</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathrm{P\text{-}GRAFT}}=\underbrace{P\,M\,T}_{\text{sampling}}\,F_{u}\;+\;\underbrace{E_{\mathrm{sft}}\,P\,K}_{\text{ training}}3F_{u},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathrm{DDPO}}=\underbrace{E_{\mathrm{ddpo}}\,N_{\mathrm{gen}}\,T}_{\text{trajectories}}\cdot(1+3)F_{u}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>DDPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ddpo</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>gen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>trajectories</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathrm{DDPO}}=\underbrace{E_{\mathrm{ddpo}}\,N_{\mathrm{gen}}\,T}_{\text{trajectories}}\cdot(1+3)F_{u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GenAI-Bench configuration.</span>
We use <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P{=}1600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P{=}1600</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}40</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{sft}}{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>sft</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{sft}}{=}10</annotation></semantics></math> for P-GRAFT;
Trajectories generated per epoch <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{gen}}{=}128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>gen</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{gen}}{=}128</annotation></semantics></math>, and Number of Epochs <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{ddpo}}{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ddpo</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{ddpo}}{=}50</annotation></semantics></math> for DDPO</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T19" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 19: </span>FLOPs in units of forward pass <math id="A5.T19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> for GenAI-Bench.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T19.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T19.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T19.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Algorithm</th>
<th id="A5.T19.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Sampling</th>
<th id="A5.T19.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Training</th>
<th id="A5.T19.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Total</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T19.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T19.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">P<span id="A5.T19.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">-GRAFT</span> (<math id="A5.T19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}10,\,M{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}10,\,M{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A5.T19.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.40\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6.40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.40\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.48\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.48\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.88\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6.88</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.88\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T19.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T19.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">P<span id="A5.T19.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">-GRAFT</span> (<math id="A5.T19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}1,\,M{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}1,\,M{=}4</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A5.T19.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A5.T19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.256\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.256</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.256\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A5.T19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.048\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.048</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.048\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="A5.T19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.304\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.304</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.304\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T19.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T19.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">DDPO (<math id="A5.T19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E{=}50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.T19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{gen}}{=}128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>gen</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{gen}}{=}128</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A5.T19.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A5.T19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.256\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.256</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.256\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A5.T19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.768\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.768</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.768\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T19.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><math id="A5.T19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.024\text{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.024</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.024\text{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discussion.</span>
P<span id="A5.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">-GRAFT</span>’s total compute is dominated by sample generation, while backpropagation is confined to fine-tuning on the selected top-<math id="A5.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> samples. In contrast, DDPO backpropagates through all <math id="A5.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denoising steps online for every sample, creating a sequential bottleneck. Consequently, despite DDPO’s nominal FLOPs appearing comparable or lower in our regime, its wall-clock time is substantially longer due to stepwise backward passes that are less parallelizable. Moreover, as shown in Table 2, P<span id="A5.SS4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">-GRAFT</span> achieves higher rewards under the reported budgets; and in the compute-matched case (<math id="A5.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>; Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ E.1.1 Different choices of 𝐾 and 𝑀 ‣ E.1 Ablations ‣ Appendix E Text-to-Image Generation ‣ Fine-Tuning Diffusion Models via Intermediate Distribution Shaping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), P<span id="A5.SS4.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">-GRAFT</span> still outperforms DDPO, indicating that gains come from improved optimization and not just additional training compute.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
